# ComfyUI Installation (Windows with Python 3.12)

This guide documents the installation of ComfyUI using the manual GitHub method on Windows.

## Prerequisites
- Windows 10/11
- Python 3.12 installed
- Git installed
- Internet connection

## Step 1: Clone the Repository
Open Command Prompt or PowerShell and run:

```bash
git clone https://github.com/comfyanonymous/ComfyUI.git
cd ComfyUI

# Step 2: Create a Virtual Environment
py -3.12 -m venv venv

# Step 3: Activate the Virtual Environment
venv\Scripts\activate

# Step 4: Upgrade pip
python -m pip install --upgrade pip

# Step 5: Install PyTorch
pip install torch torchvision torchaudio

# Step 6: Install ComfyUI Dependencies
pip install -r requirements.txt

# Step 7: Run ComfyUI (CPU Mode)
python main.py --cpu

# Step 8: Open ComfyUI
After the server starts, open the following URL in your browser:
http://127.0.0.1:8188
